## Auto-Coach — "the app does all the thinking" (✅ all 5 phases shipped 2026-06-10)

> Roadmap + the 13 hardening decisions live in `.claude/auto-coach-plan.md`. DB v16→19.
> **Status:** built + JVM-tested (269 app unit tests, ~50 of them coach); **pending on-device
> review + `connectedAndroidTest` for migrations 16→17→18→19.** Everything data-driven starts
> empty by design — shadow validation, calibration samples, and trust streaks all need real
> training weeks, so for the first month the honest output is mostly "the plan is working, no
> changes" (which is correctness, not breakage).
>
> **The loop the five phases form:** generate a pro-grade plan → per-set weight chip (calibrated
> to how you respond, capped at your dumbbells) → a **Weekly Coach Pass** each new week →
> proposes changes with plain-English reasons → apply via safe, **undoable** existing user write
> paths → a **watcher** judges whether each change landed → reverts what didn't → and, per change
> *type*, **earns** the right to auto-apply. Pure systems live in `domain/coach/`
> (`AutoCoachPlanner` · `WeeklyReview` · `SuggestionCalibrator` · `OutcomeWatcher` ·
> `TrustLedger`), impure orchestration in `data/repo/CoachRepository`. Invariants held everywhere:
> never rebuilds the program (targeted overlay/swap writes only), never touches a slot you've
> customized, and fails loud (a crashed pass is an ERROR status, never a silent HOLD).

